        }
      ]
    },
    "statement": "Assume full AC. There exist constants $\\epsilon,C>0$ such that every smooth $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ connection form $A$ near the closed Euclidean ball $\\overline B_r(x)\\subset\\mathbb R^4$ satisfying $F_A^+=0$ and $\\|F_A\\|_{L^2(B_r)}\\le\\epsilon$ obeys\n$$r^2\\|F_A\\|_{L^\\infty(B_{r/2}(x))}\\le C\\|F_A\\|_{L^2(B_r(x))}.$$\nThe constants are independent of the ball and of $A$. Here anti-self-duality and the norms use the standard Euclidean metric and orientation. No general curved-metric, perturbed or singular ASD equation, energy quantization, or removable-singularity conclusion is asserted.",
    "raw_sha256": "68aa7a6594c812682ed449a93cfb50ab7302016e21cff68362555b80bd5aa2e0"
  },
